menu "BME280 synthetic source (Labs 5 and 6)"

    config LAB_SIM_BME280
        bool "Synthetic BME280 values (bme280_sim) instead of a sensor"
        default y
        help
            Labs 5 and 6: bme280_init()/bme280_read() return synthetic
            values (slow-sine temperature 20-25 degC, pressure close to
            1013 hPa, humidity close to 45%) instead of reading a sensor.

            Lab 3 turns this off: there the students write the driver
            (main/bme280_i2c.c), which in QEMU reads the simulated
            registers of component bme280_regsim (CONFIG_LAB3_REG_SIM).

endmenu
